{"declarations":[{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/IsClass.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.isClass?\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Sym</span>.<span class=\"name\">isClass?</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">type</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Basic.html#Lean.Meta.MetaM\">MetaM</a> <span class=\"fn\">(<a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Option\">Option</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.Name\">Name</a>)</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Efficient version of `Meta.isClass?` for symbolic simulation. It does not use reduction, and it\ninstantiates metavariables only if the head of the conclusion of `type` is an assigned one.","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Sym/IsClass.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.isClass?","kind":"def","line":24,"name":"Lean.Meta.Sym.isClass?","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Meta/Sym/IsClass.lean#L24-L33"}}],"imports":["Lean.Meta.Sym.SymM"],"instances":[],"name":"Lean.Meta.Sym.IsClass"}